## Image Loading Optimization (Shimmer Skeleton + Fade-in)

### Primary Approach (User-Approved CSS)
The user explicitly provided this cleaner CSS for skeleton loading. Use `.skeleton-card` for placeholder containers and `.game-img` for image fade-in:

```css
@keyframes shimmer {
  0% { background-position: -200% 0; }
  100% { background-position: 200% 0; }
}
.skeleton-card {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #e8e8e8 25%, #f5f5f5 50%, #e8e8e8 75%);
  background-size: 200% 100%;
  animation: shimmer 1.5s infinite linear;
  border-radius: 8px;
}
.game-img { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.6s ease; }
.game-img.loaded { opacity: 1; }
```

### Alternative: Theme-matched shimmer overlay
Use when you want the shimmer to blend with a dark/colored theme background rather than light gray:

```css
